<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dingiswayo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1770–<a href="/years/1818">1818</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dingiswayo was the paramount chief of the Mthethwa in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal">KwaZulu-Natal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, from about 1795 until 1818. He organised young men into age-based regiments and extended his authority over many neighbouring chiefdoms, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a>, whose young leader Shaka served in his army. He was captured and killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwide">Zwide</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndwandwe">Ndwandwe</a>, after which Shaka took over the Mthethwa confederacy.</p></div>
